-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Page 3: the lab.js memory task
-- Headless from task-2 on, so the task takes the full viewport. task-1 keeps
-- the chrome (see above) and hides it from CSS while the experiment runs.
--
-- The Qualtrics original interleaves the vignette pauses with the memory task,
-- so the task is split into four pages with a pause survey between each:
--
--   task-1 (instr, practice, learn A) → pause-1 (vignette Franz)
--   task-2 (recall A)                 → pause-2 (vignette Geo)
--   task-3 (learn B)                  → pause-3 (vignettes Math + Deut)
--   task-4 (recall B, closing)        → questions (device, closing code)
--
-- All four task pages bind the SAME `labjs` row, so they share one data table,
-- and the study pins `labjs_response_id` in sessionStorage so every segment
-- updates one result row rather than inserting four.
