       `published_at` = NOW() WHERE id = @survey_pause2;

SET @pause_json = '{"title":{"default":"Kanji – Pause 3: Mathematik und Aufsatz","en":"Kanji – Break 3: Maths and Essay","fr":"Kanji – Pause 3: mathématiques et rédaction","it":"Kanji – Pausa 3: matematica e tema"},"locale":"de","showQuestionNumbers":"off","showProgressBar":"off","progressBarType":"pages","pages":[{"name":"pause3","elements":[{"type":"html","name":"P3_1","html":{"default":"<p><strong><br></strong></p>\\n<p><strong>Super, Sie haben jetzt alle Kanjis aus der zweiten Runde gelernt!</strong></p>\\n<p>Jetzt kommt wieder eine kleine Pause, in welcher Sie Fragen zu Ihrem Kind beantworten werden.</p>","en":"<p><strong><br></strong></p>\\n<p><strong>Great, you have now learned all the kanji from the second round!</strong></p>\\n<p>Now there will be another short break, during which you will answer questions about your child.</p>","fr":"<p><strong><br></strong></p>\\n<p><strong>Super! Vous avez maintenant appris tous les kanjis de la deuxième série.</strong></p>\\n<p>Il y aura maintenant une courte pause, pendant laquelle vous répondrez à quelques questions sur votre enfant.</p>","it":"<p><strong><br></strong></p>\\n<p><strong>Bene! Ora ha imparato tutti i kanji della seconda serie!</strong></p>\\n<p>Ci sarà ora una breve pausa, durante la quale risponderà ad alcune domande sul suo bambino.</p>"}},{"type":"html","name":"P3_2","html":{"default":"<p>Es folgen nun zwei kurze Geschichten aus dem Familienalltag. Diese beschreiben Situationen mit Ihrem Kind. Nach jeder Geschichte stehen mehrere Sätze. Diese zeigen mögliche Vorgehensweisen von Eltern.</p>\\n<p>Bitte sagen Sie wie oft jeder Satz auf Sie zutrifft. Es gibt dabei keine falsche oder richtige Antwort. Wichtig ist nur, dass Sie ehrlich einschätzen, wie Sie selbst typischerweise handeln.</p>","en":"<p>Below are some short stories from everyday family life. They describe situations involving your child. After each story, there are several sentences. These show possible ways for parents to respond.</p>\\n<p>Please say how often each sentence applies to you. There are no right or wrong answers. The important thing is that you honestly assess how you typically behave.</p>","fr":"<p>Voici maintenant de courtes histoires de la vie familiale. Elles décrivent des situations avec votre enfant. Après chaque histoire, vous trouverez plusieurs phrases qui montrent des façons possibles d\'agir des parents.</p>\\n<p>Veuillez indiquer à quelle fréquence chaque phrase vous correspond. Il n’y a pas de bonne ou de mauvaise réponse. L’important est seulement d’évaluer honnêtement comment vous agissez habituellement.</p>","it":"<p>Ora seguono brevi racconti dalla vita quotidiana di una famiglia. Queste descrivono situazioni con il proprio figlio. Dopo ogni racconto seguono diverse frasi che indicano possibili comportamenti dei genitori.<br>Vi preghiamo di indicare con quale frequenza ogni frase si applica al vostro caso. Non esistono risposte giuste o sbagliate. L\'importante è che valutiate onestamente come vi comportate di solito.</p>"}},{"type":"matrix","name":"P3_Vignette_Math","title":{"default":"<div style=\\"display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:1em;flex-wrap:wrap;\\"><div style=\\"flex:1 1 20em;min-width:14em;\\"><p><strong>Mathematik</strong></p><p>Ihr Kind hat nächste Woche einen Mathetest. Für diesen Test muss Ihr Kind zuhause üben. Manche Aufgaben kann Ihr Kind schon gut, manche Aufgaben sind aber schwierig. Ihr Kind wählt oft denselben Rechenweg aber dieser Rechenweg ist manchmal unpassend. Ihr Kind wiederholt ähnliche Fehler. Bei schwierigen Aufgaben kommt es nicht weiter.</p>\\n<p>Wie wahrscheinlich ist es, dass Sie Folgendes sagen oder tun:</p></div><img style=\\"width:200px;max-width:30%;height:auto;object-fit:contain;flex:0 0 auto;\\" src=\\"{{ASSET_BASE}}/Vignette_Math.jpg\\" alt=\\"\\"></div>","en":"<div style=\\"display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:1em;flex-wrap:wrap;\\"><div style=\\"flex:1 1 20em;min-width:14em;\\"><p><strong>Learning Math</strong></p><p>Your child has a math test next week. Your child needs to practice at home for this test. Some problems your child can already do well, but some are difficult. Your child often chooses the same method of calculation, but this method is sometimes unsuitable. Your child repeats similar mistakes. With difficult problems, your child can’t make any progress.</p>\\n<p>How likely is it that you would do or say the following?</p></div><img style=\\"width:200px;max-width:30%;height:auto;object-fit:contain;flex:0 0 auto;\\" src=\\"{{ASSET_BASE}}/Vignette_Math.jpg\\" alt=\\"\\"></div>","fr":"<div style=\\"display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:1em;flex-wrap:wrap;\\"><div style=\\"flex:1 1 20em;min-width:14em;\\"><p><strong>Mathématiques</strong> <strong></strong></p><p>Votre enfant a un test de maths la semaine prochaine. Pour ce test, il/elle doit s’exercer à la maison. Certaines tâches, il/elle les sait déjà bien faire, mais d’autres sont difficiles. Souvent, il/elle choisit toujours la même méthode de calcul, mais cette méthode n’est parfois pas adaptée. Il/elle répète des erreurs similaires. Avec les exercices difficiles, il/elle n’arrive pas à avancer.</p>\\n<p>Quelle est la probabilité que vous disiez ou faisiez ce qui suit?</p></div><img style=\\"width:200px;max-width:30%;height:auto;object-fit:contain;flex:0 0 auto;\\" src=\\"{{ASSET_BASE}}/Vignette_Math.jpg\\" alt=\\"\\"></div>","it":"<div style=\\"display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:1em;flex-wrap:wrap;\\"><div style=\\"flex:1 1 20em;min-width:14em;\\"><p><strong>Matematica</strong></p><p>Suo figlio/a ha un test di matematica la prossima settimana. Per questo test deve esercitarsi a casa. Alcuni esercizi li sa già fare bene, ma altri sono difficili. Spesso sceglie sempre lo stesso metodo di calcolo, ma a volte questo metodo non è adatto. Ripete errori simili. Con gli esercizi difficili non riesce ad andare avanti.</p>\\n<p>Quanto è probabile che lei dica o faccia quanto segue:</p></div><img style=\\"width:200px;max-width:30%;height:auto;object-fit:contain;flex:0 0 auto;\\" src=\\"{{ASSET_BASE}}/Vignette_Math.jpg\\" alt=\\"\\"></div>"},"isAllRowRequired":true,"columns":[{"value":"1","text":{"default":"Sehr unwahrscheinlich","en":"Very unlikely","fr":"Très improbable","it":"Molto improbabile"}},{"value":"2","text":{"default":"Unwahrscheinlich","en":"Unlikely","fr":"Improbable","it":"Improbabile"}},{"value":"3","text":{"default":"Vielleicht","en":"Maybe","fr":"Peut-être","it":"Forse"}},{"value":"4","text":{"default":"Wahrscheinlich","en":"Likely","fr":"Probable","it":"Probabile"}},{"value":"5","text":{"default":"Sehr wahrscheinlich","en":"Very likely","fr":"Très probable","it":"Molto probabile"}}],"rows":[{"value":"1","text":{"default":"Ich frage mein Kind auch bei richtig gelösten Aufgaben, wie es auf die Lösung gekommen ist.","en":"Even when my child has solved a problem correctly, I ask how they arrived at the solution.","fr":"Même lorsque mon enfant a bien résolu un exercice, je lui demande comment il est parvenu à la solution. ","it":"Anche quando mio figlio risolve correttamente un esercizio, gli chiedo come è arrivato alla soluzione."}},{"value":"2","text":{"default":"Ich frage mein Kind, ob es einen anderen Rechenweg ausprobieren möchte.","en":"I ask my child if they’d like to try a different method of calculation. ","fr":"Je demande à mon enfant s\'il souhaite essayer une autre méthode de calcul.  ","it":"Chiedo a mio figlio se vuole provare un altro metodo di calcolo. "}},{"value":"3","text":{"default":"Ich sage meinem Kind, dass die Geschwindigkeit ein Hinweis ist: Wenn es länger für eine Aufgabe braucht, ist das ein Hinweis, dass die Aufgabe schwierig ist.","en":"I tell my child that speed is a clue: if it takes longer to complete a problem, that’s a sign that the problem is difficult.","fr":"Je dis à mon enfant que la rapidité est un indice : s’il met plus de temps à résoudre un exercice, cela signifie que celui-ci est difficile. ","it":"Dico a mio figlio che la velocità è un indizio: se impiega più tempo per un esercizio, significa che l\'esercizio è difficile."}},{"value":"4","text":{"default":"Ich ermutige mein Kind, Rechen-Tricks anzuwenden, wie z.B. grosse Zahlen in kleine Zahlen zerlegen.","en":"I encourage my child to use math tricks, such as breaking large numbers down into smaller ones.","fr":"J’encourage mon enfant à utiliser des astuces de calcul, comme par exemple décomposer les grands nombres en petits nombres. ","it":"Incoraggio mio figlio a utilizzare trucchi di calcolo, come ad esempio scomporre i numeri grandi in numeri piccoli. "}},{"value":"5","text":{"default":"Ich lasse mein Kind selbst entscheiden, in welcher Reihenfolge es die Aufgaben macht.","en":"I let my child decide for themselves in which order to do the problems. ","fr":"Je laisse mon enfant décider lui-même de l\'ordre dans lequel il va faire les exercices. ","it":"Lascio che mio figlio decida da solo in quale ordine svolgere i compiti. "}},{"value":"6","text":{"default":"Nach dem Lernen frage ich mein Kind, wie viele Aufgaben es glaubt, richtig und allein gelöst zu haben.","en":"After studying, I ask my child how many problems they think they solved correctly on their own. ","fr":"Après la révision, je demande à mon enfant combien d\'exercices il pense avoir résolus correctement et tout seul.","it":"Dopo lo studio chiedo a mio figlio quanti compiti pensa di aver risolto correttamente e da solo. "}}]},{"type":"matrix","name":"P3_Vignette_Deut","title":{"default":"<div style=\\"display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:1em;flex-wrap:wrap;\\"><div style=\\"flex:1 1 20em;min-width:14em;\\"><p><strong>Aufsatz schreiben für den Deutschunterricht</strong></p><p>Ihr Kind hat in der Schule eine Hausaufgabe für den Deutschunterricht erhalten. Für die Aufgabe hat Ihr Kind eine Woche Zeit. Es soll einen Aufsatz über sein schönstes Ferienerlebnis schreiben. Der Aufsatz soll beschreiben, was passiert ist, wo das Erlebnis stattgefunden hat und warum es so besonders schön war. Ihrem Kind fallen viele mögliche Erlebnisse ein, sodass es sich schwer entscheiden kann. Zudem gehört Deutsch nicht zu seinen Lieblingsfächern, weshalb es eher langsam mit der Aufgabe vorankommt.</p>\\n<p>Wie wahrscheinlich ist es, dass Sie Folgendes sagen oder tun:</p></div><img style=\\"width:320px;max-width:40%;height:auto;object-fit:contain;flex:0 0 auto;\\" src=\\"{{ASSET_BASE}}/Vignette_Deut.jpg\\" alt=\\"\\"></div>","en":"<div style=\\"display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:1em;flex-wrap:wrap;\\"><div style=\\"flex:1 1 20em;min-width:14em;\\"><p><strong>Writing an Essay for German Class</strong></p><p>Your child has been assigned homework for German class. Your child has one week to complete the assignment. They are writing an essay about their best vacation experience. The essay should describe what happened, where the experience took place, and why it was so special. Your child can think of many possible experiences, making it hard to decide. Additionally, German isn’t one of their favorite subjects, which is why they’re making slow progress on the assignment.</p>\\n<p>How likely is it that you would do or say the following</p></div><img style=\\"width:320px;max-width:40%;height:auto;object-fit:contain;flex:0 0 auto;\\" src=\\"{{ASSET_BASE}}/Vignette_Deut.jpg\\" alt=\\"\\"></div>","fr":"<div style=\\"display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:1em;flex-wrap:wrap;\\"><div style=\\"flex:1 1 20em;min-width:14em;\\"><p><strong>Rédiger une dissertation pour le cours d\'allemand</strong></p><p>Votre enfant a reçu un devoir à faire à la maison pour son cours d\'allemand. Il dispose d\'une semaine pour réaliser ce devoir. Il doit rédiger une dissertation sur son plus beau souvenir de vacances. La rédaction doit décrire ce qui s\'est passé, où l\'expérience a eu lieu et pourquoi elle était si particulière. Votre enfant a tellement d\'expériences en tête qu\'il a du mal à se décider. De plus, l\'allemand ne fait pas partie de ses matières préférées, c\'est pourquoi il avance plutôt lentement dans son travail.</p>\\n<p>Quelle est la probabilité que vous disiez ou faisiez ce qui suit?</p></div><img style=\\"width:320px;max-width:40%;height:auto;object-fit:contain;flex:0 0 auto;\\" src=\\"{{ASSET_BASE}}/Vignette_Deut.jpg\\" alt=\\"\\"></div>","it":"<div style=\\"display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:1em;flex-wrap:wrap;\\"><div style=\\"flex:1 1 20em;min-width:14em;\\"><p><strong>Scrivere un tema per la lezione di tedesco</strong></p><p>Vostro figlio ha ricevuto a scuola un compito per la lezione di tedesco. Ha una settimana di tempo per svolgerlo. Deve scrivere un tema sulla sua esperienza più bella delle vacanze. Il tema deve descrivere cosa è successo, dove si è svolta l\'esperienza e perché è stata così bella. A vostro figlio vengono in mente tante esperienze possibili, tanto che fa fatica a decidere. Inoltre, il tedesco non è tra le sue materie preferite, motivo per cui procede piuttosto lentamente con il compito.</p>\\n<p>Quanto è probabile che lei dica o faccia quanto segue:</p></div><img style=\\"width:320px;max-width:40%;height:auto;object-fit:contain;flex:0 0 auto;\\" src=\\"{{ASSET_BASE}}/Vignette_Deut.jpg\\" alt=\\"\\"></div>"},"isAllRowRequired":true,"columns":[{"value":"1","text":{"default":"Sehr unwahrscheinlich","en":"Very unlikely","fr":"Très improbable","it":"Molto improbabile"}},{"value":"2","text":{"default":"Unwahrscheinlich","en":"Unlikely","fr":"Improbable","it":"Improbabile"}},{"value":"3","text":{"default":"Vielleicht","en":"Maybe","fr":"Peut-être","it":"Forse"}},{"value":"4","text":{"default":"Wahrscheinlich","en":"Likely","fr":"Probable","it":"Probabile"}},{"value":"5","text":{"default":"Sehr wahrscheinlich","en":"Very likely","fr":"Très probable","it":"Molto probabile"}}],"rows":[{"value":"1","text":{"default":"Ich ermutige mein Kind, die Geschichte vor dem Schreiben zu strukturieren, damit der Text verständlich wird.","en":"I encourage my child to outline the story before writing so that the text is easy to understand.","fr":"J\'encourage mon enfant à structurer son histoire avant de se mettre à écrire, afin que le texte soit compréhensible.","it":"Incoraggio mio figlio a strutturare la storia prima di iniziare a scrivere, in modo che il testo risulti comprensibile."}},{"value":"2","text":{"default":"Wenn mein Kind nicht weiss, wie es mit dem Schreiben beginnen soll, ermutige ich es, einen anderen Einstieg zu wählen.","en":"If my child doesn’t know how to start writing, I encourage them to choose a different opening.","fr":"Si mon enfant ne sait pas par où commencer, je l\'encourage à choisir une autre introduction.","it":"Se mio figlio non sa da dove cominciare a scrivere, lo incoraggio a scegliere un altro punto di partenza. "}},{"value":"3","text":{"default":"Ich ermutige mein Kind, zu planen, an welchen Tagen es am Aufsatz arbeitet und wann es ihn fertigstellen möchte.","en":"I encourage my child to plan which days they will work on the essay and when they want to finish it.","fr":"J\'encourage mon enfant à planifier les jours où il travaillera sur sa rédaction et la date à laquelle il souhaite la terminer. ","it":"Incoraggio mio figlio a pianificare in quali giorni lavorare al tema e quando desidera finirlo. "}},{"value":"4","text":{"default":"Ich rege mein Kind dazu an, den geschriebenen Text gründlich durchzulesen, um Fehler, Wiederholungen und Unstimmigkeiten zu entdecken.  ","en":"I encourage my child to read through the written text thoroughly to identify errors, repetitions, and inconsistencies. ","fr":"J\'incite mon enfant à relire attentivement le texte rédigé afin de repérer les erreurs, les répétitions et les incohérences.","it":"Incoraggio mio figlio a rileggere attentamente il testo scritto per individuare errori, ripetizioni e incongruenze."}},{"value":"5","text":{"default":"Ich erkläre meinem Kind, dass es mehr üben muss, wenn ihm das Schreiben schwerfällt.","en":"I explain to my child that they need to practice more if they find writing difficult","fr":"J\'explique à mon enfant qu\'il doit s\'entraîner davantage s\'il a des difficultés à écrire.","it":"Spiego a mio figlio che deve esercitarsi di più se ha difficoltà a scrivere."}},{"value":"6","text":{"default":"Ich frage mein Kind, nach dem es fertig ist, wie zufrieden es mit dem Text ist.","en":"After my child is finished, I ask them how satisfied they are with the text.","fr":"Une fois qu\'il a terminé, je demande à mon enfant s\'il est satisfait de son texte.","it":"Quando ha finito, chiedo a mio figlio quanto è soddisfatto del testo. "}}]}]}],"completedHtml":{"default":"<p>Danke! Es geht gleich weiter mit der Lernaufgabe.</p>","en":"<p>Thank you! The learning task continues shortly.</p>","fr":"<p>Merci! L\'exercice va reprendre dans un instant.</p>","it":"<p>Grazie! Il compito riprende tra poco.</p>"},"checkErrorsMode":"onValueChanged"}';
SET @pause_json = REPLACE(@pause_json, '{{ASSET_BASE}}', @asset_base);
SET @seed_title = JSON_UNQUOTE(JSON_EXTRACT(@pause_json, '$.title.default'));
SET @survey_pause3 = (SELECT id FROM `surveys`
  WHERE `survey_generated_id` = 'Kanji_Data'
    AND JSON_UNQUOTE(JSON_EXTRACT(`config`, '$.title.default')) = @seed_title
  ORDER BY id LIMIT 1);
INSERT INTO `surveys` (`survey_generated_id`, `config`, `published`, `published_at`)
SELECT 'Kanji_Data', @pause_json, @pause_json, NOW()
  WHERE @survey_pause3 IS NULL;
SET @survey_pause3 = COALESCE(@survey_pause3, LAST_INSERT_ID());
UPDATE `surveys` SET `config` = @pause_json, `published` = @pause_json,
       `published_at` = NOW() WHERE id = @survey_pause3;

-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Every survey needs a question to hold the code
--
-- url_params writes the code into the survey as `extra_param_code`, but
-- SurveyJS discards a value with no matching question, so `redirect_at_end`
-- resolved `{{extra_param_code}}` to nothing and sent the participant to a
-- URL with a trailing slash, which does not route. The question is hidden and
-- never cleared, so it survives to the redirect.
--
-- Part 1 has its own copy that mirrors ID_1; this adds one to the others.
-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------

UPDATE `surveys`
   SET `published` = JSON_ARRAY_APPEND(`published`, '$.pages[0].elements',
         JSON_OBJECT('name', 'extra_param_code', 'type', 'text', 'title', 'extra_param_code',
                'visible', CAST(FALSE AS JSON), 'clearIfInvisible', 'none')),
       `config`    = JSON_ARRAY_APPEND(`config`,    '$.pages[0].elements',
         JSON_OBJECT('name', 'extra_param_code', 'type', 'text', 'title', 'extra_param_code',
                'visible', CAST(FALSE AS JSON), 'clearIfInvisible', 'none'))
 WHERE JSON_EXTRACT(`published`, '$.title.default') IS NOT NULL
   AND JSON_UNQUOTE(JSON_EXTRACT(`published`, '$.title.default')) LIKE 'Kanji%'
   AND JSON_SEARCH(`published`, 'one', 'extra_param_code', NULL, '$.pages[*].elements[*].name') IS NULL;


-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Study content: lab.js memory task
-- {{ASSET_BASE}} is replaced with @asset_base so image paths resolve.
-- -----------------------------------------------------------------------

DELETE FROM `labjs` WHERE `labjs_generated_id` IN
  ('LABJS_KANJIADULT01',
   'Kanji_Task1','Kanji_Task2','Kanji_Task3','Kanji_Task4');

SET @study_json = '{"components":{"c1":{"title":"Resume","type":"lab.html.Screen","content":"<div class=\\"kanji-stage\\"></div>","timeout":"1","files":[],"responses":[],"parameters":[],"messageHandlers":[{"message":"run","code":"try {\\n  const KEY = \'kanji_labjs_response_id\';\\n  const stored = window.sessionStorage.getItem(KEY);\\n  if (stored) {\\n    labjs_response_id = stored;\\n  } else if (typeof labjs_response_id === \'string\' && labjs_response_id) {\\n    window.sessionStorage.setItem(KEY, labjs_response_id);\\n  }\\n} catch (e) {\\n  // sessionStorage unavailable (private mode): fall back to a\\n  // per-page id. The segments then save as separate rows, which\\n  // is recoverable by joining on the participant code.\\n}\\n"}]},"c2":{"title":"Instruction instr_learn 1","type":"lab.html.Screen","content":"<div class=\\"kanji-stage kanji-instr\\"><div class=\\"kanji-instr-body\\" id=\\"instrBody\\"></div><button type=\\"button\\" class=\\"kanji-next\\" id=\\"instrNext\\"></button></div>","files":[],"responses":[],"messageHandlers":[{"message":"run","code":"const screen = this;\\nconst el = this.options.el;\\nconst texts   = {\\"de\\":\\"<b>Nun kommt die Lernaufgabe.</b> <ul> <li>Wenn Sie jetzt weiter drücken, geht die Lernaufgabe los! </li> <li>Sie können die Aufgabe nicht unterbrechen / pausieren. </li> <li>Sie benötigen ca. 15 min Zeit. </li> </ul> <b>Drücken Sie erst auf weiter, wenn Sie bereit sind! </b>\\",\\"en\\":\\"<b>The learning task will start next.</b> <ul> <li>When you continue, the task will begin!</li> <li>You cannot interrupt or pause the task.</li> <li>You will need approximately 15 minutes to complete it.</li> </ul> <br type=\\\\\\"_moz\\\\\\" /> <b>Only press continue when you are ready! </b>\\",\\"fr\\":\\"<p data-end=\\\\\\"152\\\\\\" data-start=\\\\\\"106\\\\\\"> </p> <p data-end=\\\\\\"152\\\\\\" data-start=\\\\\\"106\\\\\\"><b>L&rsquo;exercice d&rsquo;apprentissage va commencer.</b></p> <ul> <li data-end=\\\\\\"330\\\\\\" data-start=\\\\\\"154\\\\\\">Lorsque vous continuerez, l&rsquo;exercice d&eacute;butera.</li> <li data-end=\\\\\\"330\\\\\\" data-start=\\\\\\"154\\\\\\">Vous ne pourrez pas interrompre ou mettre l&rsquo;exercice en pause.</li> <li data-end=\\\\\\"330\\\\\\" data-start=\\\\\\"154\\\\\\">Vous aurez besoin d&rsquo;environ 15 minutes pour le terminer.</li> </ul> <b>N&#39;appuyez sur Continuer que lorsque vous &ecirc;tes pr&ecirc;t! </b>\\",\\"it\\":\\"<p data-start=\\\\\\"56\\\\\\" data-end=\\\\\\"101\\\\\\"> <b>Ora inizia il compito di apprendimento.</b></p> <ul> <li data-start=\\\\\\"56\\\\\\" data-end=\\\\\\"101\\\\\\">Quando preme Avanti, il compito avrà inizio.</li> <li data-start=\\\\\\"56\\\\\\" data-end=\\\\\\"101\\\\\\">Non potrà interrompere o mettere in pausa il compito.</li> <li data-start=\\\\\\"56\\\\\\" data-end=\\\\\\"101\\\\\\">Avrà bisogno di circa 15 minuti per completarlo.</li> </ul> <b>Premete “avanti” solo quando siete pronti!</b>\\"};\\nconst labels  = {\\"de\\":\\"Weiter\\",\\"en\\":\\"Next\\",\\"fr\\":\\"Suivant\\",\\"it\\":\\"Avanti\\"};\\nconst lang    = (window.KANJI_LANG || (((document.querySelector(\'[class*=selfHelp-locale-]\') || {}).className || \'\').match(/selfHelp-locale-([a-z]{2})/) || [])[1] || \'de\');\\nlet html      = texts[lang] || texts.de;\\n// resolve {{IMG:name}} against the study\'s file pool\\nhtml = html.replace(/\\\\{\\\\{IMG:([^}]+)\\\\}\\\\}/g, (m, name) => {\\n  const src = screen.files[name];\\n  return src ? \'<img class=\\"kanji-instr-img\\" src=\\"\' + src + \'\\">\' : \'\';\\n});\\nel.querySelector(\'#instrBody\').innerHTML = html;\\nconst btn = el.querySelector(\'#instrNext\');\\nbtn.textContent = labels[lang] || labels.de;\\nbtn.addEventListener(\'click\', () => screen.respond(\'next\'));\\n"}],"parameters":[]},"c3":{"title":"Instruction instr_learn 2","type":"lab.html.Screen","content":"<div class=\\"kanji-stage kanji-instr\\"><div class=\\"kanji-instr-body\\" id=\\"instrBody\\"></div><button type=\\"button\\" class=\